    "b-ks2-path-sync-intro": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-sync-intro",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Initial, manual, and automatic epoch Sync run mechanical intake and the configured per-game source pipeline before accepting their boundary. Mechanical intake reconciles target identity and unchanged-code citations, then imports attempt evidence. The source pipeline separately records acquisition, archival import, search indexing, and optional curation. Manual publication performs intake after the checkout repoint and before its durable publication boundary and dispatch release."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ks2-path-sync-intro-detail-1": {
      "id": "b-ks2-path-sync-intro-detail-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Bootstrap seeds every enabled source. Incremental Sync follows each source definition: each_sync sources refresh every time, while explicit sources reuse accepted captures until requested. A wiki mirror import reads a local export and does not claim a fresh upstream download. Importers preserve cited records and queue pr_imported or archival_ingest tasks. Required source stages gate acceptance; optional semantic curation remains visible as pending until an enabled librarian consumer or manual drain processes the queue."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
